# Every file is checked out exactly as committed, whatever core.autocrlf
# says. Git for Windows sets autocrlf=true system-wide, which turns the
# patch queue, the shell scripts and the INFs into CRLF: prepare-qemu.sh
# then fails with "patch does not apply" and bash with "$'\r': command not
# found". The few files committed with CRLF (the 9x DDK headers, reference
# logs) keep theirs. Submodules are not covered; build-windows.sh checks
# them (docs/build-windows.md).
* -text
